They are kept as close to upstream as practical so they stay diffable
against it. Local additions sit in separate files:

  internal/tui/render/nav_api.go       chrome renderers for this project
  internal/tui/render/theme_api.go     theme accessors for this project
  internal/tui/render/calendar_api.go  the calendar entry points

The package comments in internal/tui/render/doc.go and
internal/tui/render/habit/doc.go say the same thing at the source, and
everything else in those directories, including the tests, is this
project's own.

Two copied functions carry a deliberate change, both in nav.go:
renderTopRule hardcoded the HEY wordmark and takes a title instead, and
renderNavLabel underlines a digit shortcut as a prefix rather than wherever
the digit happens to occur inside the label.

The directories were once named after where the code came from, and are
not any more: internal/tui/heyui is now internal/tui/render, and
internal/habit is now internal/tui/render/habit. The names say what the
packages do; this file says where they came from.

This project once followed HEY's workflow and no longer does: the screener,
the Imbox, the Feed and the Paper Trail have been removed, and what remains
